From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Winter <danielwinterw@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:41:40 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: expose Laya decision reads

Compile the self-contained Laya runtime into libllama and expose it through a
narrow Skippy ABI: open a Laya GGUF, report its sequence budgets and special
tokens, tokenize with its own Metaspace + BPE tokenizer, and run one packed
forward pass that returns raw scorer and action-head logits per question.

The runtime keeps its weights on the first accelerator when one exists and
schedules with the CPU backend behind it, so any unsupported op falls back.
Thread count is set through the backend registry so libllama does not link
ggml-cpu directly.
